      "side": 1,
      "message": "Because I can\u0027t add new enums to `enum binder_work_type` without breaking the KMI:\n```\n  type \u0027enum binder_work_type\u0027 changed\n    enumerator \u0027BINDER_WORK_FROZEN_BINDER\u0027 (10) was added\n    enumerator \u0027BINDER_WORK_CLEAR_FREEZE_NOTIFICATION\u0027 (11) was added\n```\n\nSo this needs to be parsed into a generic int in order to process the new different types defined outside the enum:\n```\n#define BINDER_WORK_FROZEN_BINDER\t\t(BINDER_WORK_CLEAR_DEATH_NOTIFICATION + 1)\n#define BINDER_WORK_CLEAR_FREEZE_NOTIFICATION\t(BINDER_WORK_FROZEN_BINDER + 1)\n```\n\nWe could simply drop this hack and override the KMI report CR -2. I only wanted to prove a clean KMI report first.",
